<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX1-QA2-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX1-QA2-001" ;
  triage:title "AX.1 QA-2 re-assessment: Herdr-backed end-to-end AC4 coverage still missing in crates/atm-core/tests/nudge_mode.rs (ATM-QA-001 not resolved by the fix pass)" ;
  triage:description "Sprint AX.1 Required validation asks that for one Herdr-backed and one tmux-backed member, atm send resolves Delivery/DeliveryAck, atm queue resolves Queue/QueueAck, and a --task-id send resolves Task (six assertions per backend), plus the marker assertion for the tmux member and the NudgeKind::Queue graft-dispatch assertion on the sync and async write paths. At b6fd3c743 (PR #1185 QA-2) crates/atm-core/tests/nudge_mode.rs roster_member() (line ~190) is hardcoded to harness: RosterHarness::PythonGraft, so no Herdr-backed roster member exists in the file. tmux_and_herdr_delivery_families_share_the_nudge_kind_table (line ~556) loops over the string labels tmux/herdr while calling the backend-independent pure function built_in_nudge_template_kind_from_post_send_event; it never exercises a real Herdr-backed member through hook.rs's local_herdr_post_send / HerdrNudgeTarget dispatch branch with marker + NudgeKind::Queue graft-dispatch + PreparedWrite.outbound_request.nudge_mode == Deferred assertions. This is a new record filed after the fix-pass Completion (c3, 2026-09-05T06:02:09Z) so that the AX1 Completion is invalidated; the original record ATM-QA-001 (QA-1) stays untouched. Fixed since QA-1 and not part of this finding: Deferred on both prepare paths, AC3 snapshot. Reviewer disagreement (req-qa open vs rust-qa-agent resolved) was settled by quality-mgr reading the test code. Report: PR #1185 comment 5549901700." ;
